message.content:
Review a rewrite of the Fortress revival's batch workflow before a batch (7b) runs under it tonight. Work in `/home/user/fortress` on `main`; read only, except for one file you write and commit.

## What was done

`explorations/coordinator/postmortem-2026-09-29/synthesis.md` specifies a new batch practice (section 1), four defaults (section 2), the changes with quoted anchors (section 4) and what stays (section 5). An Opus worker implemented section 4 in seven commits, `3a4aabdd3` through `fe5eaee2e`; `git diff 4bdcb9d20 fe5eaee2e` is the whole change (about 210 lines added, 256 removed, in `climb-batch-workflow.js`, `climb-batch-workflow.md`, `protocol.md`, `PLAN.md`, `FACTS.md`/`FACTS-history.md`, two files with a false attribution removed, and `mg-run.sh` moved to `explorations/coordinator/tools/`). Items 63-64 (batch 7b's record) and 65 (POSITIONS) were not the rewriter's.

The rewriter's own account of where it read an item differently from its text, which you are to judge:
- item 11 not done, its anchor being inside batch 6.5's embedded manifest; the same sentence for 7b is in `explorations/compile-ladder/plan-7b/manifest/gen7b.py:235`, left for 7b's record;
- item 8: the rung worker may also land the decision record its tail asks for;
- item 13: a `testIsStage` rung always starts the distance stage in the background;
- item 17: the ladder driver `run-subset.sh` is copied into `tmp/SLUG/ladder/` because it writes into its own tracked folder;
- item 28: the gather takes `record.md` back out of the index after folding it;
- items 31-32: the review's checks renumbered, `checkerRows` removed, the count-table check moved to the post-batch review;
- item 34: the judge runs whenever `blockingCode` is non-empty; routed findings `review-routed.N`; a text-mismatch test now routed, not blocking;
- items 36 and 39: the background microGPT start is the commit stage's step 4, also when the push is held; `mg-run.sh`'s timeout is 5,400 s against measured runs of 4,761 and 4,792 s;
- the merged-tree repair's test-run captures moved under `tmp/gate-batch-<N>/`;
- left conflicting: home 2's "the report cites both captures" against "never cite a file under tmp/".

## Your question

Does the rewritten script, run as batch 7b's workflow tonight, do what the synthesis's sections 1 and 2 say, with nothing the synthesis removed still happening, nothing it keeps (section 5) lost, and no path through the stages that stalls, loops, renders a prompt with `undefined`, commits scratch, or lands without the gate? Read the synthesis's sections 1, 2, 4 and 5 and the diff, and the script only around the changed stages and the recovery texts; do not read the 380 KB script whole. Judge each of the rewriter's readings above: sound, or a defect with its fix.

Run scenarios on a scratch copy, never on the tracked script: the rewriter left a stub harness at `/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-fortress/fe616d40-a9c6-56d7-9da1-7168a172765d/scratchpad/rewrite/` (`stubrun.js`, `check.sh`, `out7b/`), which splices batch 7b's generated block and walks seven merged-tree cases. Read it, run it, and add the cases you think it misses (for example: a rung whose skeptic refuses twice; a rung dropped; a red gate the judge cannot answer; a code finding whose repair turns the gate red; a process stop resumed with `resumeFromRunId` mid-commit). `explorations/compile-ladder/plan-n/manifest/checkn.js` is batch N's older harness and expects the removed second review; do not treat its failure as a finding. Also run the harness-style parse of the script (FACTS, "`node --check` does not check the batch script as the Workflow harness parses it").

Measure nothing the record holds; run no `ant`, no Fortress program.

## Output

Write `explorations/coordinator/postmortem-2026-09-29/script-review.md`: the findings, most severe first, each with where (file and quoted anchor), what goes wrong, and the fix in a sentence or two; then the rewriter's readings judged one line each; then the scenarios run and their results. Plain register, no tables, no model identifiers. Commit only that file: `git add -- <path> && git commit -m "<message>" -- <path>`, the message ending with exactly these two lines after a blank line:

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AmiXNpJxQ6TBwec4vJZHDB

Do not push. Return the commit hash and the findings in one line each, marked blocking (must be fixed before 7b launches) or not.
